.claude/worktrees/

# Run output: state.json is tracked (it drives the progress page); the
# generated page and most screenshot evidence are regenerable, so they are not.
# `shots/*` and not `shots/`: git does not descend into an ignored DIRECTORY,
# so a negation under a `.gauntlet/shots/` rule re-includes nothing and
# `git add -A` stages only this file. It looks like it worked. Ignore the
# directory's CONTENTS and the negation can reach inside.
.gauntlet/shots/*
.gauntlet/progress.html

# EXCEPT the shell run, which is graded evidence rather than a regenerable
# picture. "Regenerable" was true and beside the point: a critic asked to open
# these found nine stale shots and a 47-check `route.json` with pre-fix wordings
# sitting where a 74-check run should have been, and — the part that matters —
# `09-bombed-keeps-its-own-exit.png` was a bomb-out screen with NO EXIT ON IT,
# filed next to a record saying that check passed. That is the exact false pass
# the opacity fix was written to kill, preserved as its own refutation, and no
# reader could date it because a screenshot carries no provenance.
#
# The GDD logged this once already (§ the "photographed" sentence naming a
# gitignored artifact). Logging it twice and ignoring it a third time is not a
# policy. `route.json` now carries `capturedFrom` — commit, branch, dirty state —
# so these are datable; 380K is a cheap price for evidence a grader can check
# instead of trust.
!.gauntlet/shots/shell/

# Same argument for the cut-in run: `frames.json` records eight checks a critic
# is asked to read, and `CutInView.tsx` cites this directory by name — the
# sentence that was false until the pictures were committed.
!.gauntlet/shots/cutin/

# And the cut-in CAP run, which is the strongest of the three: `cap.json` is the
# only artifact in this repository that shows GDD §12.3's refusal condition
# being ENFORCED BY THE RUNNING APP rather than scanned for in source. The
# regexes that used to pin it all survive the mutation that breaks it. A record
# of an executed refusal is exactly the thing the two paragraphs above argue
# must be gradeable rather than regenerable — and it is the record that dates
# WHICH build was played, which no amount of re-running recovers after the fact.
!.gauntlet/shots/cutin-cap/

# And the meet SOUND run, which is the only record of the half of GDD §12.2's
# bar — "pacing AND sound" — that no screenshot can hold. `sound.json` carries
# the wall-clock instant every cue reached the audio layer, per beat, with each
# file's own decoded length, so it is the only artifact that can show a cue
# firing again while the last copy is still sounding.
#
# It was untracked for the round in which it found exactly that: five 180ms
# rattles inside 149ms, from a bar-load loop asking for one every 90. A finding
# that lives only in a console someone happened to read is the same failure mode
# as an undatable screenshot, one channel over.
#
# THE RECORD, AND NOT THE DIRECTORY — which is where this one differs from the
# three above, on their own stated reason rather than on their form. Each of
# those tracks a dated record plus the pictures that record describes. This
# directory is shared by two tools: `sound.json` is the dated record
# (`capturedFrom`, per-check `failures`, a `REQUIRED_SHOT_RECORDS` row), and
# `capture-meet.mjs`'s 21 PNGs and `frames.json` are the other tool's raw dump —
# no `capturedFrom`, no checks, in no required list, checked by nothing. A
# directory-wide negation here tracked the record and un-ignored the dump, so
# `git status` was never empty again and every evidence bundle from then on
# stamped DIRTY. That is the staleness instrument grading itself unusable, which
# costs more than the 900K it saves.
!.gauntlet/shots/meet/
.gauntlet/shots/meet/*
!.gauntlet/shots/meet/sound.json

# G.2D member-card dues line. Critics cannot pass the player-facing copy on
# FloorGrid source order; this folder holds the dated 390×844 photograph and
# the `dues.json` record of the drawn text.
!.gauntlet/shots/g2d/
.gauntlet/shots/g2d/*
!.gauntlet/shots/g2d/dues.json
!.gauntlet/shots/g2d/390x844-member-dues.png

# SF-TWL-GYM-EMPIRE-UX-01 player-facing vertical-slice evidence. Before/after
# 390×844 photographs of Play (grid hidden), Build (grid on), Shop, Staff, More.
!.gauntlet/shots/empire-ux-01/
